From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: sun60i-a733: fix UART0 pin group

The A733 UART0 is routed to PB9 (TX) and PB10 (RX), matching the
A733 datasheet and the mainline Linux device tree. The U-Boot DT
incorrectly described the group as PB0/PB1, which makes the U-Boot
proper console reconfigure the wrong pins and emit garbage after the
early banner.

Signed-off-by: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -152,5 +152,5 @@
 			uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
-				pins = "PB0", "PB1";
+				pins = "PB9", "PB10";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
 				function = "uart0";
 			};
